-- title:
--   Injectivity of the coordinate map on adic points of widehatΩ
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain), $K$ a field that is its fraction field, $\pi$ an element of $\mathcal{O}$, and $C$ a field which is a $K$-algebra carrying a valuation $v$ with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$; let $R$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra equipped with an algebra map to $C$, all the scalar actions being compatible. Let $\varpi$ be a pseudo-uniformizer of $K$ for $C$, that is an element $\varpi.\varpi \in K$ whose valuation in $C$ satisfies $0 < v < 1$ and such that for every $a \in K^{\times}$ there is $N$ with $v(\varpi.\varpi)^N \le v(a) \le v(\varpi.\varpi)^{-N}$. Assume `IsAdicFrame π ϖ R`: $\pi$ is irreducible; $R \to C$ is injective with image exactly $\{c \in C : v(c) \le 1\}$; $R$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$; an element of $K$ has valuation $\le 1$ in $C$ exactly when it comes from $\mathcal{O}$; the image of $K$ in $C$ is closed; and the images of $\pi$ and of $\varpi.\varpi$ in $C$ coincide. Then the map sending an adic point $x$ of the formal upper half plane over $R$ — a family of Deligne data $x.\mathrm{pt}(n)$ over the quotients $R/(\pi^{n+1})$, each assigning to every full $\mathcal{O}$-lattice $M \subset K^2$ a submodule of the base change of $M$ with invertible quotient, compatibly with inclusions, equivariantly for homotheties and nondegenerately at every prime, these data being compatible under the transition maps — to its coordinate $x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C \in C$, namely the unique $z \in C$ with $(z,1)$ in the $C$-span of the image of `AdicPoint.stdLine` in $C^2$ when such a $z$ exists uniquely and $0$ otherwise, is injective.
--
--   This is the injectivity half of the identification of the $\mathcal{O}_C$-points of the formal upper half plane $\widehat{\Omega}$ with the points of the rigid-analytic upper half plane $\Omega$ over $C$, in the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of $p$-adic uniformisation: although the line at the standard lattice at a single level does not determine the datum, the whole compatible system of lines at the standard lattice does determine the lines at all lattices. It is used in the results on covering $\Omega$ by finitely many chart unit loci and on invariant pullbacks for the Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalOmega_AdicPoint_toOmega_injective.lean

